1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,908
A hundred pounds a month,

2
00:00:01,908 --> 00:00:03,632
invested for twenty years.

3
00:00:03,632 --> 00:00:06,483
That's twenty-four thousand pounds paid in.

4
00:00:06,483 --> 00:00:08,339
At four per cent after fees,

5
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:10,859
it grows to about thirty-six thousand,

6
00:00:10,859 --> 00:00:11,787
seven hundred.

7
00:00:11,787 --> 00:00:12,848
At six per cent,

8
00:00:12,848 --> 00:00:14,108
forty-six thousand,

9
00:00:14,108 --> 00:00:14,904
two hundred.

10
00:00:14,904 --> 00:00:16,097
At seven per cent,

11
00:00:16,097 --> 00:00:17,357
fifty-two thousand,

12
00:00:17,357 --> 00:00:18,153
one hundred.

13
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:19,280
Or overpay a five

14
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,004
per cent mortgage instead,

15
00:00:21,004 --> 00:00:22,794
and after twenty years your

16
00:00:22,794 --> 00:00:24,783
balance is forty-one thousand,

17
00:00:24,783 --> 00:00:26,441
one hundred pounds lower.

18
00:00:26,441 --> 00:00:27,170
Guaranteed.

19
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,828
So investing only wins if

20
00:00:28,828 --> 00:00:30,685
it beats your mortgage rate,

21
00:00:30,685 --> 00:00:31,414
after fees.
